<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pedro de Cevallos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1715">1715</a>–<a href="/years/1778">1778</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pedro de Cevallos was a Spanish soldier and colonial administrator. As governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a> from 1757 he captured the Portuguese outpost of Colonia del Sacramento in 1762. In 1776 he led a great expedition to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-la-plata">Río de la Plata</a>, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santa-catarina">Santa Catarina</a> island and Colonia again, and became the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> of the new Viceroyalty of the Río de la Plata.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pedro-de-cevallos.jpg" alt="Pedro de Cevallos" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pedro_de_Cevallos.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
